> **SELF-EXCLUSION.** QoDuck is a real stealth model on Alibaba's Qoder platform (launched 2026-11-07) but **no model card, weights, API identifier, parameter count, licence, context figure or benchmark has been published** by Alibaba/Qwen/Qoder or any third party. With zero verified numbers on any axis, no 1–100 scores are filed; the notes below are the verified facts only.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** QoDuck ("a stealth model whose identity has yet to be disclosed" — Qoder's own words)
- **Short description:** Alibaba/Qoder's anonymous coding-and-reasoning stealth preview inside Qoder desktop; the only firm facts are operational (free allowance), not technical.
- **Provider / access:** Qoder International app only (individual accounts). Officially: IDE, JetBrains plugin and CLI do **not** support the promotion; Teams/Enterprise customers do not see it. No public API, no endpoint, no weights.
- **Release / knowledge:** promotion started 2026-11-07 (Singapore time); end date "yet to be determined". Knowledge cutoff not published.
- **IDs:** none published (`opencode/qoduck` is the dataset route).
- **Context window:** not published by Qoder; community claims of ~1M are unverified (the folder's curated metadata lists 1,048,576 — unsourced).
- **Modalities:** not published; text in/out assumed only.
- **Pricing:** free daily allowance for individuals during the promo (credit rate 0.5× → 0.0×, including at the highest thinking intensity; resets daily); after the allowance 0.5×, or switch models. Qoder's 0.5× rate card is the tier it applies to Qwen3.8-Max / DeepSeek-V4-Pro (flagship tier).
- **Architecture:** undisclosed. Community hypotheses (Qwen4-27B dense + n-gram table, Qwen tokenizer fingerprint, ~35 GB at Q8, ~480 tok/s) are unverified hearsay; a vendor-side kernel PR mentions "Qwen4-27B dense" but no checkpoint ran end-to-end. Qwen 4 itself remains unshipped (Alibaba: in training).

